Article 2 (Eligibility to Apply for Selection as Clerks and Prosecution Investigators)
(1) Persons eligible to apply for selection as clerks of military courts and prosecution clerks of military prosecution (hereinafter referred to as "clerks") shall fall under any of the following: <Amended on January 3, 2023.>
1. Commissioned officers of the legal branch (excluding military legal officers), warrant officers, or noncommissioned officers;
2. Civilian military employees serving in any of the following institutions, units or departments:
(a) Military courts;
(b) The Ministry of National Defense Prosecutors' Office;
(c) Military Prosecutors' Offices of each armed service;
(d) Legal affairs offices at the headquarters of each armed service;
(e) Legal affairs departments of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, the Republic of Korea-United States Combined Forces Command, units and agencies directly under the Ministry of National Defense, or units belonging to each armed service;
3. Officers, warrant officers, noncommissioned officers, or civilian military employees who have completed a prescribed course of legal education and graduated from a junior college under Article 2 of the Higher Education Act or a school of equivalent or higher level;
4. Persons who have completed a noncommissioned officer training course for the legal branch of an armed service.
(2) Persons eligible to apply for selection as prosecution investigators of military prosecution (hereinafter referred to as "prosecution investigators") shall have served as clerks for at least three years: Provided, That the Chief of Staff of each armed service may determine a different period where deemed necessary in consideration of personnel management and other circumstances of the armed service.
